From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:56:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 316/342] net_server: DHCP never waits past the end of a state

After five tries, socket_timeout::Shift() waited at least 60 s (RFC 2131
4.4.5's minimum for renewing and rebinding), however close the end of the
state was. With a 60 s lease, renewal started at 30 s and its last wait ran
to about 105 s: past the rebinding time (52 s) and the end of the lease. A
wireless bridge that leases 60 s and ignores renewals sent to it then
refused the late rebinding, and the client started over about every 90 s
(a C2 behind such a bridge). Every wait now ends with its state, so
rebinding broadcasts while the lease is still valid. Rebooting now ends at
REBOOT_TIMEOUT as intended, not about 6 s after it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/servers/net/DHCPClient.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/servers/net/DHCPClient.cpp b/src/servers/net/DHCPClient.cpp
index eb2d5dd55d..04bc58773c 100644
--- a/src/servers/net/DHCPClient.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/net/DHCPClient.cpp
@@ -455,8 +455,8 @@ socket_timeout::Shift(int socket, bigtime_t stateMaxTime, const char* device)
 
 	tries++;
 
+	bigtime_t now = system_time();
 	if (tries > MAX_RETRIES) {
-		bigtime_t now = system_time();
 		if (stateMaxTime == -1 || stateMaxTime < now)
 			return false;
 		bigtime_t remaining = (stateMaxTime - now) / 2 + 1;
@@ -467,6 +467,12 @@ socket_timeout::Shift(int socket, bigtime_t stateMaxTime, const char* device)
 	if (timeout > AS_USECS(MAX_TIMEOUT))
 		timeout = AS_USECS(MAX_TIMEOUT);
 
+	// Never wait past the end of the state: with a short lease, the 60 s
+	// above would carry renewing past the rebinding time, and rebinding past
+	// the end of the lease. Just after the end, the next timeout moves on.
+	if (stateMaxTime != -1 && now + timeout > stateMaxTime)
+		timeout = std::max(stateMaxTime - now, bigtime_t(0)) + 1000;
+
 	syslog(LOG_DEBUG, "%s: Timeout shift: %" B_PRIdTIME " msecs (try %" B_PRIu8 ")\n",
 		device, timeout / 1000, tries);
 
